findings.citation_text:
6-301.12 Observed the hand sink in the ladies restroom to be out of hand towels. Hand towels were supplied to the restroom. 
Each HAND WASHING SINK or group of adjacent HAND WASHING SINKS shall be provided with:
(A) Individual, disposable towels; 
(B) A continuous towel system that supplies the user with a
clean towel;
(C) A heated-air hand drying device; 
(D) A hand drying device that employs an air-knife system that delivers high velocity, pressurized air at ambient temperatures.
Reference 6-301.12

findings.comment:
750.800b - The following food contact surfaces were soiled:
A) BAR - 1. pizza oven (food debris);
2. pizza slicer (grease); &
3. soda gun on right side of ice bin at the south end of the bar (mold);

B) KITCHEN - 1. can opener blade (food debris) & 2. pizza oven (carbon/food debris).

Properly clean and sanitize food contact surfaces between uses/as needed, up to every 4hrs after continuous use, to prevent cross contamination and eliminate buildup of debris.

750.800e - The following non-food contact surfaces were soiled:
A) BAR - 1. plastic storage bins to the left of pizza freezer (outer surfaces - splash/buildup) &
2. tracks of sliding door cooler (general debris);

B) STORAGE AREA - bottom inside upright meat freezer (splash)

C) KITCHEN - 1. soiled dish storage table (splash/food debris);
2. chemical storage shelving & black crate holding bug spray (general buildup);
3. flat grill in corner next to fryer (drip tray - heavy grease/scrapings); &
4. fryers - general surfaces and inside bottom compartments where mechanicals are located (grease/food debris). 

Clean non-food contact surfaces daily/as needed to eliminate buildup of debris.
